  "title": "Introduction to Microsoft Fabric Data Agents",
  "description": "Are Microsoft Fabric Data Agents just another buzzword, or can they actually change how your users get answers from their data? In this video, Mitchell Pearson walks through what Fabric Data Agents are, how they use generative AI to power Q&A over your data, and how you can get started in just a few minutes once your data is in Fabric.\n\nYou\u2019ll see how to connect a semantic model, choose which tables and columns are exposed, and ask natural-language questions like \u201cWhat are my total sales by year?\u201d\u2014then inspect the exact DAX Copilot generates behind the scenes. Mitchell also covers the key prerequisites (F2+ Fabric capacity and tenant settings), why good data modeling and \u201cprep for AI\u201d are critical, and how to publish agents so users can reach them from places like Microsoft 365 Copilot or via a Copilot Studio hub agent in Teams.\n\nIf your organization is moving to Fabric and you want to unlock AI-powered self-service analytics\u2014not just more reports\u2014this is a great place to start. If you\u2019d like help migrating to Fabric or building out data agents, reach out to us at Pragmatic Works for training and consulting.\n\n\ud83d\udc49 On-Demand Learning - Start With The FREE Community Plan: https://prag.works/odl-trial-yt\n\n\ud83d\udd17Pragmatic Works On-Demand Learning Packages: https://pragmaticworks.com/pricing/\n\ud83d\udd17Pragmatic Works Boot Camps: https://pragmaticworks.com/boot-camps/\n\ud83d\udd17Pragmatic Works Hackathons: https://pragmaticworks.com/private-tr...\n\ud83d\udd17Pragmatic Works Virtual Mentoring: https://pragmaticworks.com/virtual-me...\n\ud83d\udd17Pragmatic Works Enterprise Private Training: https://pragmaticworks.com/private-tr...\n\ud83d\udd17Pragmatic Works Blog: http://blog.pragmaticworks.com/\n\n00:00 \u2013 Why Fabric Data Agents Matter (and Why They\u2019re Less Scary Than They Sound)\n00:21 \u2013 What Are Microsoft Fabric Data Agents?\n01:12 \u2013 Prerequisites: Capacity, Tenant Settings, and Semantic Models\n02:46 \u2013 Creating Your First Data Agent in a Fabric Workspace\n03:43 \u2013 Connecting Data Sources and Choosing Tables & Columns\n05:23 \u2013 Asking Natural-Language Questions and Reviewing the DAX\n07:18 \u2013 From Proof of Concept to Real Projects (Migration & Data Prep)\n08:14 \u2013 Publishing Agents to M365 Copilot and Teams via Copilot Studio\n09:38 \u2013 Where You Can Consume Fabric Data Agents Today\n10:32 \u2013 Wrap-Up and What\u2019s Next in the Data Agents Series\n\nLet's connect:\n\n\u2714\ufe0fDiscord: https://prag.works/yt-discord\n\u2714\ufe0fFacebook: https://prag.works/yt-fb\n\u2714\ufe0fInstagram: https://prag.works/yt-insta\n\u2714\ufe0fLinkedIn: https://prag.works/yt-li\n \nPragmatic Works\n350 Governor St, Suite 300, Green Cove Springs, FL 32043\nPhone: (904) 638-5743\nEmail: training@pragmaticworks.com\n#PragmaticWorks",
